//!
//! # Sparse files
//!
//! A sparse member is read where its map takes a shape every reader extracts
//! alike: see [`Sparse`](crate::Sparse) and [`SparseFlaw`](crate::SparseFlaw).
//! A real size of 2<sup>60</sup> or more is refused, as bsdtar fails at it
//! ([`RealSize`](crate::SparseFlaw::RealSize)). A map larger than
//! [`Limits::metadata`](crate::Limits::metadata) (1 MiB by default) is
//! refused ([`MapLimit`](crate::SparseFlaw::MapLimit)), as Go refuses one past
//! the same size.
//!
//! | Archive | GNU tar | bsdtar | Python | Go | ferrotape | Cases |
//! | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
