//!
//! # Global headers
//!
//! A global header's records apply to every later member for GNU tar and
//! Python, and to none for Go. [`GlobalHeaders`](crate::GlobalHeaders)
//! chooses which family a program reads as, or refuses a global header
//! holding any record but `comment` (the default). bsdtar applied none as
//! well until libarchive 3.8.10. From that release, it refuses an archive
//! from a global header holding any record but `comment` on, wherever it
//! falls. There, [`Defer`](crate::GlobalHeaders::Defer) reads as Go alone
//! does.
//!
//! | Archive | GNU tar | bsdtar | Python | Go | ferrotape | Cases |
//! | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
//! | A global header holding any record but `comment` | applies its records | refuses the archive from that header on, listing only the members before it | applies its records | applies none | Refuse: refused ([`GlobalRecord`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalRecord)). Apply: applied, as GNU tar and Python apply it. Defer: none applied, as Go reads it | `global/global-owner-names`, `global/a-global-link-target`, `global/a-global-path-each-member-overrides`, `global/a-global-header-in-a-v7-header`, `global/a-global-hdrcharset`, `global/a-global-path-after-a-member`, `global/a-global-path-after-the-last-member` |
//! | A global header giving a keyword twice, with different values | applies the first | refuses the archive | applies the last | applies neither | Refuse: refused ([`GlobalRecord`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalRecord)) unless the keyword is `comment`. Apply: refused ([`RepeatedKeyword`](crate::ErrorKind::RepeatedKeyword)). Defer: Strict refused, as for a member's own header, Compatible none applied | `global/a-global-path-given-twice`, `global/a-global-link-target-given-twice` |
//! | A global header with no records | reads on | fails there, extracting nothing after it | reads on | reads on | refused in every mode ([`EmptyMetadata`](crate::ErrorKind::EmptyMetadata)) | `global/an-empty-global-header` |
//! | A global `size`, a vendor keyword, an empty value, or a second global header once one has set a member's record | reads them otherwise than Python. Replaces an earlier global header's records | refuses the archive from that header on | reads them otherwise than GNU tar. Merges a later global header's records with the earlier's | applies none | Refuse and Apply: refused ([`GlobalRecord`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalRecord), [`SecondGlobal`](crate::ErrorKind::SecondGlobal)). Defer: none applied | `global/a-global-size-and-path`, `global/a-global-extended-attribute`, `global/an-empty-global-uid-after-a-global-uid` |
//! | A global header while a pax header, a long name, a long link or another global header waits for its member | reads on, otherwise than Python | fails on two global headers in a row | reads on, otherwise than GNU tar | lets a global header consume a waiting pax header | refused in every mode ([`GlobalBetweenMetadata`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalBetweenMetadata), [`RepeatedMetadata`](crate::ErrorKind::RepeatedMetadata)) | `global/two-global-headers-before-a-member`, `global/two-global-comments-before-a-member`, `global/a-global-header-after-a-pax-header` |
